; Rembrandt, "Christ Crucified between the Two Thieves: The Three Crosses"
; (Bartsch 78, New Hollstein 274): ten impressions in four collections.
; Two impressions of a second plate, "Christ Presented to the People"
; (Bartsch 76, New Hollstein 290), so that plates can differ.
;
; Every row below is transcribed by hand from a public collection record.
; SOURCES.md gives the URL and the wording for each one. Nothing here is
; extracted automatically and nothing is inferred: where a record does not
; state something, there is no row.

; --- Levels ---------------------------------------------------------------
; Three sorts, one per level at which a print can be "the same".

(sort Sheet)   ; one impression: a sheet held by one collection
(sort State)   ; a state of the plate
(sort Plate)   ; the copper plate, through all its states

; A plate is not a catalogue entry. Catalogue numbers are names that
; catalogues give to plates. No record here individuates plates in any
; other way, so the audit can show two catalogues disagreeing about a
; plate; it cannot show a catalogue being wrong about one.

; A sheet is given by the name its holder's inventory gives it.
(constructor sheet (String) Sheet)

; The two abstractions. Congruence makes them go upward only:
; same sheet => same state => same plate, never the reverse.
(constructor state-of (Sheet) State)
(constructor plate-of (State) Plate)

; --- Records --------------------------------------------------------------
; The number is only there to list each pair of records once.

(relation record (String i64))

(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-OB-616" 1)
(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-OB-617" 2)
(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-OB-618" 3)
(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-1962-39" 4)
(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-1962-40" 5)
(record "met/41.1.31" 6)
(record "met/41.1.32" 7)
(record "met/41.1.33" 8)
(record "ngv/1971-4" 9)
(record "cleveland/1959.241" 10)
(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-OB-611" 11)
(record "rijksmuseum/RP-P-1975-1" 12)

